286
00:20:16,840 --> 00:20:19,900
While multi-million dollar yachts rely on water delivery,

287
00:20:20,500 --> 00:20:24,080
a different kind of multi-million dollar merchandise delivers by air.

288
00:20:24,820 --> 00:20:28,420
Tech Sutton Forwarding Company specializes in shipping prize thoroughbreds

289
00:20:28,421 --> 00:20:30,580
across the U.S. and parts of Canada.

290
00:20:31,420 --> 00:20:35,000
The company is part of an industry that ships billions of dollars of horses

291
00:20:35,001 --> 00:20:37,540
to racetracks throughout the world every year.

292
00:20:37,541 --> 00:20:46,780
Tech Sutton usually starts at places like Winding Oaks Farm in Ocala, Florida.

293
00:20:47,420 --> 00:20:51,200
The horses are led out of their barns and onto trailers bound for the airport.

294
00:20:52,540 --> 00:20:57,460
These horses are making a cross-country trip to Santa Anita Park in Arcadia, California.

295
00:21:00,680 --> 00:21:06,380
When they get to the airport, the trucks drive directly onto the airfield and park next to the company's plane.

296
00:21:07,540 --> 00:21:12,540
Each year, the company picks up and delivers about 3,000 horses.

297
00:21:12,541 --> 00:21:17,540
And six other companies throughout the U.S. provide similar services.

298
00:21:17,541 --> 00:21:22,540
This is just a regular cargo plane, and it's actually been retrofitted for the horses.

299
00:21:22,541 --> 00:21:25,540
Inside the plane's basically set up like a horse truck.

300
00:21:25,541 --> 00:21:29,540
Each position will hold three horses.

301
00:21:29,541 --> 00:21:38,040
Tech Sutton redesigned a Boeing 727, installing 21 air stalls, similar to the horse trailers

302
00:21:38,041 --> 00:21:40,420
used for ground transport.

303
00:21:40,421 --> 00:21:44,840
The back of the plane is outfitted with 16 seats for the Tech Sutton crew and trainers

304
00:21:44,841 --> 00:21:49,160
that go along for the ride.

305
00:21:49,161 --> 00:21:53,460
Handlers load the horses according to how they'll unload them at the destination.

306
00:21:53,461 --> 00:21:58,220
If one truck is picking up five, I'll try to group them all together if I can.

307
00:21:58,221 --> 00:22:04,240
And if we have to, we can put them in different spots up in the plane and wiggle them around.

308
00:22:04,241 --> 00:22:10,200
And we just chain their halters, chain on each side of their halters.

309
00:22:10,201 --> 00:22:15,460
Each stall comes with in-flight meals, and workers distribute water twice during the

310
00:22:15,461 --> 00:22:17,460
trip.

311
00:22:17,461 --> 00:22:21,660
As if they were riding in trailers, the horses will stand in these stalls for the entire

312
00:22:21,661 --> 00:22:22,660
flight.

313
00:22:22,661 --> 00:22:25,300
Most of the horses that travel on the plane

314
00:22:25,320 --> 00:22:27,700
have been traveling their whole lives,

315
00:22:27,740 --> 00:22:29,600
and so once they get in the plane,

316
00:22:29,640 --> 00:22:31,500
it's actually a lot quieter

317
00:22:31,540 --> 00:22:33,500
and a lot more enjoyable for them.

318
00:22:34,980 --> 00:22:36,840
Still, workers see their share

319
00:22:36,880 --> 00:22:39,180
of problematic four-legged passengers.

320
00:22:40,520 --> 00:22:42,280
Take your hat.

321
00:22:42,320 --> 00:22:44,320
That's what she did to his face.

322
00:22:44,340 --> 00:22:45,980
She head-butted him.

323
00:22:46,020 --> 00:22:48,680
I tried to catch the horse very close with my hand,

324
00:22:48,720 --> 00:22:50,580
and he just moved the hat so fast

325
00:22:50,620 --> 00:22:52,660
that he hit me with the hat.

326
00:22:52,661 --> 00:22:58,160
Some horses get anxious, so veterinarians will administer tranquilizers to them.

327
00:22:59,160 --> 00:23:01,660
The sedatives are mild, just to take the edge off.

328
00:23:03,160 --> 00:23:07,160
But sometimes that isn't enough, and horses must be removed from the flight.

329
00:23:08,660 --> 00:23:12,660
When all horses are loaded and accounted for, the plane makes the five-hour trip.

330
00:23:13,160 --> 00:23:17,160
When we ship the big stallions that are worth, in the hundreds of millions,

331
00:23:17,161 --> 00:23:21,160
there would be a bit more pressure than your just everyday-type racehorses.

332
00:23:21,161 --> 00:23:23,767
horses. The procedure's the same, though.

333
00:23:23,768 --> 00:23:27,200
We're just happier at the end of the job when they get

334
00:23:27,201 --> 00:23:30,795
to where they're going safely. Or relieved, I should say.

335
00:23:30,796 --> 00:23:32,940
After the plane lands, the horse's

336
00:23:32,941 --> 00:23:37,580
next stop is their barns at Santa Anita Park, where they'll wait until it's time to race.

337
00:23:45,680 --> 00:23:50,760
At home, you might not need a million-dollar delivery, but something that turns an evening in

